{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src",
    // `@urcolor/*` ships `src` beside `dist` and lists the `bun` condition
    // before `types` in its `exports`. This repo compiles with
    // `customConditions: ["bun"]` — that is how a workspace package resolves a
    // sibling's TypeScript source — so tsc follows the same condition into
    // *upstream's* source and typechecks it against this repo's flags, which
    // are stricter than upstream's own: `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` rejects
    // its `ColorNameResolution`, and `noImplicitAny` rejects the generated
    // `data/uwdata/*.js` chunks it imports without declarations. `skipLibCheck`
    // does not help — those are `.ts` program inputs, not libs.
    //
    // The mapping is **extensionless on purpose**, and that is the whole
    // ruling. `paths` is read by Bun's runtime and bundler as well as by tsc,
    // and every value that named a file satisfied one reader and broke the
    // other: pointed at `dist/index.d.ts`, `bun test` and `check-size` tried to
    // execute a declaration file ("Could not resolve ./color/color"); pointed
    // at `dist/index.js`, tsc stopped finding types at all — TS7016 on every
    // import in the package. Extensionless, each reader appends the extension
    // it wants — tsc takes `dist/index.d.ts`, Bun takes `dist/index.js` — and
    // one value serves both.
    //
    // Nothing a consumer installs changes: `paths` is a compile-time and
    // dev-time concern, and the emitted `.d.ts` still imports `@urcolor/core`
    // by name.
    //
    // Delete this block once `@urcolor/*` lists `types` before `bun` in its
    // `exports`. tsc reads conditions in order and would then take the
    // declarations on its own, while Bun, which ignores `types`, would keep
    // taking `src`. That ordering is right for a dependency; the opposite
    // ordering this repo uses for its own packages exists because a package
    // emitting its own `.d.ts` into `dist` hits TS5055 when tsc pulls that
    // sibling file into the program that produces it.
    "paths": {
      "@urcolor/core": ["./node_modules/@urcolor/core/dist/index"],
      "@urcolor/i18n": ["./node_modules/@urcolor/i18n/dist/index"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"]
}
